  # Website Build Prompt — Xplore Automations

Use this as a single, complete brief to build the site (feed it to a dev, an AI builder, or use it yourself as a spec).

## 1. Company Overview
- **Name:** Xplore Automations
- **What we do:** We build and deploy AI-powered systems for businesses.
- **Services offered (5 total):**
  1. AI Automations (workflow/process automation)
  2. AI Call Agents (voice agents)
  3. AI Chatbots
  4. Websites
  5. Apps

The site should clearly explain, for each service, what it is and what Xplore Automations builds/delivers as part of it.

## 2. Site Structure
Build as a **single-page site** (one-pager) with anchor-linked sections, in this order:

1. **Hero / Home** — company intro + a prominent **"Book a Call"** button
2. **Services** — overview of all 5 services
3. **Project Library** — portfolio section, organized **by service**
4. **Testimonials / Client Reviews**
5. **Video Testimonial** — placeholder slot
6. **Pricing**
7. **Footer** — with booking CTA repeated

*(No blog section — removed from scope.)*

## 3. Project Library (Portfolio)
- One portfolio "library" per service (Automations, Call Agents, Chatbots, Websites, Apps).
- Each library is filterable/tabbed by service, so a visitor interested in, say, AI Automations clicks that tab and only sees automation-related dummy projects.
- Populate each with a few placeholder/dummy project cards (name, short description, thumbnail, "view project" link) — to be swapped with real case studies later.

## 4. Testimonials Section
- **~10–15 client reviews total**, distributed across all 5 services.
- Include **at least 1 review for the Apps service** and **2–3 reviews specifically for the AI Chatbots service**.
- Content themes to include:
  - Voice/Call Agent reviews: emphasize that the AI call agent **doesn't miss/lose a single lead** and handles calls smoothly.
  - Website reviews: emphasize **speed, responsiveness, and functionality** of the sites built.
  - AI Chatbot reviews (2–3): emphasize things like fast response times, handling customer queries 24/7, reducing support workload, and improving customer engagement/conversions.
  - Automation/App reviews: general satisfaction, time saved, results.
- **Important constraint:** Do **not** use real people's names, photos, or LinkedIn profiles for these — attributing invented quotes to real, identifiable individuals without their consent is misleading and can cause real problems (for them and for you). Instead use **realistic fictional clients** (invented name, role, company, initials-based or generic avatar). Swap in genuine client reviews once you've collected real ones.
- **Video testimonial:** Leave one clearly marked placeholder slot on the page for a **real client video** (e.g., "Client success story — video coming soon"), which you will personally film and upload later.

## 5. Blog Section
- Add a blog grid/list on the page with a handful of dummy posts (title, excerpt, date, "read more").
- Every blog post's cover/wallpaper image should have the **Xplore Automations logo watermarked in the bottom-right corner**.

## 6. Pricing
- Applies **per service** — pricing must be shown separately for each of the 5 services (Automations, Call Agents, Chatbots, Websites, Apps).
- **Two plans per service:**
  1. **Advanced Plan** — show a **dummy fixed price**.
  2. **Custom Plan** — no price shown; instead a **"Book a Call"** button.
- **Navigation flow:** Home page has a general "Pricing" link/section. Client clicks Pricing → sees all 5 services listed → clicks the specific service (e.g., "Voice Agents") → sees that service's pricing detail (Advanced price + Custom/Book a Call option). So it's not one flat price list — it's service-specific pricing pages/panels.

## 7. Booking
- A **"Book a Call"** call-to-action should appear:
  - On the **homepage/hero** (primary placement)
  - On every **Custom Plan** pricing card
  - Ideally also repeated in the footer
- For now this can link to a placeholder booking page/anchor (e.g., a Calendly-style embed slot) to be connected later.

## 8. Design Notes
- Match the visual theme/style of the reference site you cloned from GitHub (if you want this replicated exactly, share that repo/site and it can be used as the visual reference).
- Keep the layout clean and conversion-focused: Hero → Services → Portfolio → Proof (testimonials/video) → Pricing → Book a Call.

